{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Dynamics can be associated either with a note or a general musical direction. To avoid inconsistencies between"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and among the letter abbreviations for dynamics (what is sf vs. sfz, standing alone or with a trailing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dynamic that is not always piano), we use the actual letters as the names of these dynamic elements. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other-dynamics element allows other dynamic marks that are not covered here. Dynamics elements may also be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"combined to create marks not covered by a single element, such as sfmp."}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDynamics"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Structure","symbolKind":"struct","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL11MXLDynamicsV","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLDynamics"}],"title":"MXLDynamics","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLDynamics"}]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLDynamics","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"These letter dynamic symbols are separated from crescendo, decrescendo, and wedge indications. Dynamic"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"representation is inconsistent in scores. Many things are assumed by the composer and left out, such as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"returns to original dynamics. The MusicXML format captures what is in the score, but does not try to be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"optimal for analysis or synthesis of dynamics."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The placement attribute is used when the dynamics are associated with a note. It is ignored when the dynamics"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are associated with a direction. In that case the direction element’s placement attribute is used instead."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps the MusicXML "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<dynamics>"},{"type":"text","text":" element."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldynamics"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"]]},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDynamics\/init(id:items:position:font:color:halign:valign:placement:underline:overline:lineThrough:enclosure:)"],"anchor":"Initializers","generated":true,"title":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDynamics\/color","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDynamics\/enclosure","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDynamics\/font","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDynamics\/halign","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDynamics\/id","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDynamics\/items","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDynamics\/lineThrough","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDynamics\/overline","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDynamics\/placement","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDynamics\/position","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDynamics\/underline","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDynamics\/valign"],"anchor":"Instance-Properties","generated":true,"title":"Instance Properties"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentatio